    "reject-second-borrow": {
      "hash": "c9469d55ae281e8353fa8aea43bcde3bac8dd08647e55ecdf31640ac67d2f188",
      "note": "",
      "reasons": [
        "unclear"
      ],
      "source": "## Which line does the compiler reject? {type=single tags=borrowing}\n\n```rust\nfn main() {\n    let mut v = vec![1, 2, 3];\n    let a = &mut v;\n    let b = &mut v;\n    a.push(4);\n    b.push(5);\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] `let a = &mut v;`\n- [x] `let b = &mut v;`\n- [ ] `a.push(4);`\n- [ ] `b.push(5);`\n\n::: explanation\n`a` is still used by `a.push(4)`, so the second mutable borrow on the line `let b = &mut v;` is rejected (E0499: more than one mutable borrow at a time).\n:::\n",
      "verdict": "fix"
    },
